CyberSaathi – Sample Data and Test Cases

Purpose

This document contains sample inputs and test cases used to evaluate the functionality of the CyberSaathi cyber safety application.

Sample Data

The application is tested using safe demonstration URLs, suspicious-pattern examples, invalid inputs, and empty inputs.

Test Cases

1. Suspicious URL detection – Expected: High-Risk Alert.
2. Safe demonstration URL – Expected: Low-Risk Alert.
3. Empty input – Expected: Validation message.
4. Invalid URL – Expected: Invalid URL message.
5. Check Safety button – Expected: Risk analysis executed.
6. Clear button – Expected: Input and results cleared.
7. Fake KYC-themed URL – Expected: High-Risk Alert.
8. Prize scam-themed URL – Expected: High-Risk Alert.

Testing Result

The application is evaluated based on whether the displayed output matches the expected result for each test case.

Disclaimer

The sample URLs are intended for educational and demonstration purposes only. Risk alerts depend on the application's implemented detection rules and do not guarantee website safety.
